  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be the plane containing the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#8467;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#8467;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>So, the normal vector of plane parallel to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#8467;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#8467;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Hence, the equation of plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;which passes through origin,</p><p>So,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now solving,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;distance of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;Point of intersection will be of given planes<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>Hence, distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Option (B) is correct.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}